  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nhttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/#stop-parsing has steps like:\n>3. [Update the current document readiness](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#update-the-current-document-readiness) to \"interactive\".\n \n>9. 1. [Update the current document readiness](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#update-the-current-document-readiness) to \"complete\".\n\nThe algorithms that invoke this algorithm are all part of using a parser. The only other algorithm that invokes \"Update the current document readiness\" is https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/#abort-a-parser, which also is part of interacting with a document's active parser.\n\nHowever, https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/#navigate-html explicitly does not create a parser for the about:blank document. How should the steps related to finishing parsing be integrated with the document lifecycle for about:blank?",
